## Resolution (non-finding)

**is_terminal_reply=false**: correct behaviour. The loop exits at line 1112 of
`exp2_interactive_smoke.py` when `last_slot == "verify"`, which is the intended
clean exit after the model produces a polished report. The "terminal" slot only
fires under budget pressure. All 4 agents show the same pattern.

**n_plants/f1/tp/fp/fn all None**: expected by design. The runner writes minimal
RunRecord files; evaluation against the reference ground truth is a separate step
(`make evaluate-all-records`) not yet run on any SOTA arm. `measurements.jsonl`
has 0 Exp2/3 entries. The 26-row count comes from `_count_markdown_table_rows()`
in the summary writer — it counts markdown pipe-table lines in the output, not
from comparison to the reference. Ticket 0270 (score_mechanical.py) will be the
first code to compute accuracy on SOTA arms.

**Qwen 2 turns**: correct. Qwen produced a `report`-classified output on the
designed_prompt turn (turn 1), so the loop fired `verify` immediately and exited.
No third turn was queued.

**Side finding (non-blocking)**: Anthropic turn_01 has `finish_reason: max_tokens`.
Phase A designed max_tokens=16000 with thinking=true; combined thinking+output
tokens hit the cap on the planning turn. Recovery worked — turn_02 produced a
report, turn_03 verified it. The same pattern will recur on N=2 since Phase A
will again design 16k. Noted for expectation-setting, not a blocker.

## Original exit criteria (all resolved)

- [x] Root cause of `is_terminal_reply` never being set to `true`: confirmed
      correct — verify-slot exit is the normal clean exit path.
- [x] The `None` metrics discrepancy explained: evaluation step not yet run;
      26-row count is from markdown line counting, not reference comparison.
- [x] Expected behaviour confirmed; no code change needed.
